Consult THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md and the component-specific notices.

2. Permission

You may use, study, copy, modify, combine and redistribute the covered material,
including as part of commercial products, provided that you satisfy the
attribution requirements below. You may choose terms for your own additions,
but must not remove these requirements from the covered material.

3. Required attribution

When reusing covered code, keep this license and the relevant copyright notices
with the reused material, and identify the source project and repository:

    This project uses code from toboo by Myoossootis and contributors.
    https://github.com/Myoossootis/Toboo

Place this attribution in the consuming project's README, acknowledgements or
third-party notices. If you distribute a binary without source, include it in
the accompanying documentation, license notices or an accessible About page.
For private projects, a notice retained in the private project is sufficient;
you are not required to publish private source code or private project details.

If a paper, report, presentation or public project description describes work
that incorporates covered code, cite toboo and the repository URL in its
references or acknowledgements. Adding the version or commit used is
recommended for reproducibility, but is not a condition of this license.

Merely running an unmodified application does not require a public citation.
Independent implementations of ideas without copying covered material are not
subject to these attribution requirements. This license does not restrict uses
that do not require copyright permission under applicable law.

4. Separate and earlier grants

This license does not replace a component's separate license or withdraw rights
